# Every committed blob in this repository is already LF. What was not pinned is
# the checkout: git's core.autocrlf is true on at least one machine here, so
# forty of the ninety eight tracked files arrive in the working tree with CRLF,
# and `biome check` refuses six of them on that alone. `bun run lint` is named in
# the definition of done in CLAUDE.md and could not pass on a Windows checkout.
#
# This changes no file's content. It changes what checkout writes, so the working
# tree matches the blobs that were always there.
#
# Diagnosed twice and wrongly the second time: a `grep -q $'\r'` used to check
# this reported zero CRLF files on a tree where python counted forty. Byte counts
# are the check, not grep.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Lockfiles and dumps are written by tools rather than by people.
bun.lock text eol=lf
*.sql text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf

# Anything genuinely binary, so no conversion is attempted on it.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
